## What this predicate means

**A `is-mentioned-by` B** — B makes a passing reference to A (inverse of `mentions`).  The backlink direction: a memorial enumerating which other memorials reference it incidentally.

Less commonly declared than the forward direction; most reverse-mention queries are computed via the substrate's reverse-attribute lookup (`:_mm.memory/mentions`).

