## Formal ontology mappings

Aligned predicates from established formal vocabularies:

- **CiTO** — no canonical inverse-predicate name (CiTO doesn't reify the inverse of `cito:mentions`; reverse-attribute lookup via SPARQL is the standard mechanism)
- **PROV-O** — no direct equivalent (PROV-O uses qualified-pattern reification for inverses)
- **OWL** `owl:inverseOf` — provides the META-relation; sandbar declares `:mm.memory/is-mentioned-by` as `inverse-of :mm.memory/mentions`

The pattern: backlink predicates are usually NOT first-class in formal vocabularies because reverse-attribute traversal (RDF graph patterns) provides them computationally.  Sandbar reifies them for substrate-introspection convenience (cheaper to ask "what mentions me?" without a graph-walk).

